# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
#
# Hand DomA's first virtio NIC to the radio HAL as buried_eth0.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS
# ---------------
# The product inherits minradio through
#     device/epam/aosp-xenvm-trout/aosp_xenvm_trout_arm64.mk
#       -> device/google/trout/aosp_trout_arm64.mk
#         -> device/google/cuttlefish/vsoc_arm64_only/auto/aosp_cf.mk
#           -> device/google/cuttlefish/shared/auto/device_vendor.mk
#              PRODUCT_PACKAGES += com.android.hardware.radio.minradio.virtual
#
# minradio's data implementation does not invent an interface. It hard-codes one:
#
#     radio/aidl/minradio/minradio-example/impl/RadioData.cpp
#       bool ifaceOk = netdevice::setAddr4("buried_eth0", "192.168.97.2", 30);
#       ifaceOk = ifaceOk && netdevice::up("buried_eth0");
#       if (!ifaceOk) {
#           respond()->setupDataCallResponse(
#               errorResponse(serial, RadioError::INTERNAL_ERR), {});
#           return ok();
#       }
#       ...
#       .ifname = "buried_eth0",
#
# On cuttlefish that interface exists because com.google.cf.wifi renames eth0 to
# it. Everything needed for that is installed here too -- the APEX, the binary,
# and the rc that starts it:
#
#     /apex/com.google.cf.wifi/bin/rename_netiface
#     /apex/com.google.cf.wifi/etc/com.google.cf.wifi.rc
#         service rename_eth0 .../rename_netiface eth0 buried_eth0
#             user root
#             oneshot                      <- no class, no trigger of its own
#     /vendor/etc/init/init.cutf_cvm.rc    (built from cuttlefish's
#                                           shared/config/init.vendor.rc)
#         on post-fs-data && property:ro.vendor.disable_rename_eth0=
#             wait /sys/class/net/eth0
#             start rename_eth0
#
# WHY THIS ONLY MATTERS FROM ANDROID 17
# -------------------------------------
# The disabled trigger is not new -- trout has set the property since the 15 era --
# and neither is the hard-coded interface name: cuttlefish's own reference-ril
# hard-codes it too (guest/hals/ril/reference-ril/reference-ril.c:62
# `#define PPP_TTY_PATH_ETH0 "buried_eth0"`). What changed is that until 17 no radio
# HAL on this product ever asked for the interface:
#
#   Android 15  hardware/interfaces/radio/aidl/minradio does not exist, and
#               device/google/cuttlefish/shared/auto/device_vendor.mk mentions
#               minradio nowhere. trout keeps TARGET_USES_CF_RILD ?= false
#               (aosp_trout_arm64.mk:19), so the cuttlefish RIL is not installed
#               either. Nothing attempts a data call, so nothing needs buried_eth0
#               and the disabled rename is invisible.
#
#   Android 17  device/google/cuttlefish/shared/auto/device_vendor.mk:209-212
#               "Telephony: Use Minradio RIL instead of Cuttlefish RIL" --
#               TARGET_USES_CF_RILD := false, PRODUCT_PACKAGES +=
#               com.android.hardware.radio.minradio.virtual (+
#               ConnectivityOverlayMinradio). minradio publishes IRadioData/slot1
#               and its setupDataCall requires buried_eth0.
#
# So the three preconditions -- a radio HAL that requires the interface, a trout
# property that keeps it from being created, and a failure response the framework
# retries -- first line up in 17. Nothing about this board or Xen is involved.
#
# TROUT TURNS THAT TRIGGER OFF ON PURPOSE, and that is the whole reason this file
# exists:
#
#     device/google/trout/aosp_trout_common.mk:59
#         PRODUCT_VENDOR_PROPERTIES += ro.vendor.disable_rename_eth0=true
#     device/google/trout/aosp_trout_arm64.mk:80
#         PRODUCT_PROPERTY_OVERRIDES += ro.vendor.disable_rename_eth0?=true
#
# The trigger is written to fire only while that property is EMPTY, so with
# `true` it never runs. Measured on hardware: `getprop
# ro.vendor.disable_rename_eth0` is `true`, `/vendor/etc/init/init.cutf_cvm.rc`
# does carry the block at line 57, and eth0 keeps its own DHCP lease. The service
# has no second route either -- AOSP's init.rc issues class_start for early_hal,
# hal, core, main, late_start and charger but never for `default`, which is the
# class a service with no `class` line lands in (init/service.cpp:172). So the
# only thing missing is somebody saying `start`.
#
# Trout sets the property because trout wants eth0 for its own virtwifi
# (DEVICE_VIRTWIFI_PORT := eth0, two lines above it). Overriding that is
# deliberate here, for two reasons measured on this board:
#   - trout's virtwifi does not actually produce a wlan0 on this product. Its
#     setup service is a oneshot that runs `cmd wifi set-wifi-enabled` /
#     `connect-network VirtWifi`, and cuttlefish's setup_wifi, which is what
#     creates the interface, is gated on ro.boot.wifi_impl=virt_wifi -- empty
#     here. There is no wlan0 to protect.
#   - doma.cfg gives DomA two vifs on the same bridge, so eth0 and eth1 were both
#     taking a lease out of 192.168.10.0/24 (.14 and .13) and
#     ConnectivityService carried two ETHERNET networks, one of which never
#     validated. Spending one of them on the radio HAL removes that duplication.
#     eth1 keeps .13, which is the address dnsmasq reserves for DomA and the one
#     adb connects to.
# Clearing the property instead of starting the service was considered and
# rejected: aosp_trout_common.mk sets it with an unconditional `+=` into
# PRODUCT_VENDOR_PROPERTIES, so a later assignment does not remove it.
#
# WHAT GOES WRONG WITHOUT IT
# --------------------------
# Measured on a 4 GiB board 2026-08-17, AAOS 17. setupDataCall fails and the
# failure response is the empty one above -- no cause, no suggestedRetryTime --
# so the framework reads it as an unknown, immediately retryable error:
#
#     E minradio: ioctl(8916) failed: No such device   (0x8916 = SIOCSIFADDR)
#     D RILJ    : [1006]< SETUP_DATA_CALL error 38     (38 = INTERNAL_ERR)
#     D DN-40963-C: ConnectingState: onSetupResponse: RESULT_ERROR_ILLEGAL_STATE
#     D DN-40964-C: ConnectingState: onSetupResponse: RESULT_ERROR_ILLEGAL_STATE
#
# The DataNetwork id climbs with every attempt, at roughly 7 to 13 Hz. In the
# shipping state it did not converge: DomA burned 186 % of one physical core for
# 1 h 42 m (xl list CPU 11,385 s over 6,120 s of wall clock, com.android.phone 64
# min cumulative) with nothing on screen and nobody interacting, dragging
# system_server, netd -- which respawned iptables-restore and ip6tables-restore
# to 1 m 46 s each -- resolv and ConnectivityService along with it. Screen
# transitions are slow because there is no CPU left for them.
#
# Two things it is NOT, both checked so nobody spends time on them again:
#   - Not the VINTF warnings for IRadioMessaging / IRadioVoice / IRadioIms.
#     minradio declares only config, data, modem, network and sim, so the RIL
#     leaves those three proxies null and carries on, by design.
#   - Not the radio HAL dying and being rebound. Measured while the loop was
#     running: the minradio pid never changes, its ETIME only increases, and
#     binderDied / resetProxy / "Radio Available" appear zero times in 30 s.
#     The retry is entirely on the framework side.
#
# A V4H board on the same AAOS 17, the same trout product and the same
# ro.vendor.disable_rename_eth0=true is idle -- but only by accident. It reaches
# carrierId 2256 exactly as this board does and then stops one step earlier
# because its APN database is empty (`content://telephony/carriers` returns 0
# rows against 3652 here), so no data call is ever attempted. Give that board an
# apns-conf.xml and it meets this bug too. This fix does not depend on the APN
# database, the carrier match or the preferred APN, which is why it is the one
# worth carrying.
#
# WHY `on boot`
# -------------
# rename_netiface uses SIOCSIFNAME, which needs the interface administratively
# DOWN, so this has to run after the virtio NIC exists and before anything
# configures it. Boot timings from this board (ro.boottime.*):
#
#     early-init  2.91 s
#     init        5.72 s
#     apexd       8.26 s   <- APEX rc parsed, so rename_eth0 exists from here on
#     zygote-start / netd  13.29 s / 13.28 s
#     EthernetService brings eth0 up   ~200 s (dumpsys connectivity, created
#                                              199564 ms)
#
# `on boot` fires at about 13 s. Verified on a fresh DomA boot: at uptime 19.9 s
# eth0 was present and `state DOWN`, and the rename succeeded at 26.2 s. The
# margin to the far end is over three minutes. `wait` mirrors what cuttlefish
# does in init.cutf_cvm.rc and costs nothing when the NIC is already there.
#
# Result, on a fresh boot with telephony left enabled:
#     DomA CPU, idle          186 %  ->  10.4 %  of one physical core
#     all domains, idle      57.2 %  ->   8.3 %  of the four physical cores
#     mDataConnectionState        0  ->   2      (CONNECTED)
#     ioctl(8916) / INTERNAL_ERR  ~7 Hz -> none

on boot
    wait /sys/class/net/eth0
    start rename_eth0
